# Pencil → Component Matching

Used by the `pencil-handoff` skill and `/pencil-to-code` command. Decides which component a Pencil node should map to and enforces token discipline.

## Decision Order

1. **Exact library match** — if the consuming repo's `packages/components` exports a component whose API covers the Pencil node, use it unmodified.
2. **Composition of primitives** — if no exact match, compose from existing primitives (`Card`, `Stack`, `Inline`, `Text`, `Icon`) before creating anything new.
3. **New component** — only if 1 and 2 are impossible. Place new components in the consuming repo, never in this `design-specs` repo. Document the rationale in the handoff summary.

## Default Mapping Table

| Pencil node signal | Component | Library path |
|---|---|---|
| Frame named `KPI` / number + delta + label | `KpiCard` | `packages/components` |
| Frame named `Card` / elevated surface with content | `Card` | `packages/components` |
| Rectangle + text, `layout: horizontal`, clickable | `Button` | `packages/components` |
| Icon-only clickable square ≤48×48 | `IconButton` | `packages/components` |
| Grid of cells with header row | `DataTable` | `packages/components` |
| Text + underline + input cursor | `Input` | `packages/components` |
| Rectangle with `value` + chevron | `Select` | `packages/components` |
| Segmented pills, one active | `SegmentedControl` | `packages/components` |
| Track + handle(s) | `Slider` | `packages/components` |
| Pill with status color | `Badge` | `packages/components` |
| Toast/inline info strip | `Alert` | `packages/components` |
| Modal frame over overlay | `Modal` | `packages/components` |
| Tab bar + panel | `Tabs` | `packages/components` |
| Line/area/bar chart frame | `Chart` (variant prop) | `packages/components` |
| Sparkline inside a row | `Sparkline` | `packages/components` |
| Donut/gauge | `Donut` / `Gauge` | `packages/components` |
| Step dots with labels | `StepIndicator` | `packages/components` |
| Horizontal scrubber with handles | `TimelineScrubber` | `packages/components` |

If a mapping isn't listed here, consult `.design-system/reference/design-tokens-spec.md` §2 (Component Tokens) and §3 (Data Visualization Tokens) — the section names are the canonical component names.

## Token Discipline

- **Colors** — resolve every `$token` in the `.pen` `variables` map to a semantic token in the token spec. Use CSS custom properties (`var(--color-accent-primary)`) or the Tailwind preset, never literal hex.
- **Spacing** — 4px grid only. Pencil values must map to `space.1`…`space.12`.
- **Radius** — `radius.sm | md | lg | pill | full` only.
- **Typography** — `Heebo` for UI and numerics, `Cormorant Garamond` for headings. Size/weight must map to a semantic type style (see `design-tokens-spec.md` §5).
- **Shadows** — `shadow.sm | md | lg | xl`; never custom `box-shadow`.
- **Dark mode** — if a Pencil variable defines both light and dark values, the generated code must consume the CSS variable so it auto-switches; do not branch on `dark:` class prefixes for token-covered values.

## Text & Content

- Copy labels, numbers, and captions verbatim from the `.pen`.
- Do not invent placeholder copy. If a node has no text, render nothing (or pass a required prop).
- Format numbers with the rules in `vega/rules/ui/data-formatting.md`.

## State Coverage

Every interactive component must render: `default`, `hover`, `focus-visible`, `active`, `disabled`, and (where relevant) `loading`, `empty`, `error`, `success`. Pull state-specific tokens from `02-components-and-states.json`.

## Accessibility Gates

- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for body text, ≥ 3:1 for large text and non-text UI — verify via `vega check-contrast` or `vega/tools.py:check_contrast`.
- Interactive elements ≥ 44×44px touch target.
- Semantic HTML first (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`), ARIA only to fill gaps.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for any animation derived from a Pencil transition.

## Hard Rules

- ❌ Never modify a library component to match a Pencil design — raise the mismatch as an open question instead.
- ❌ Never hardcode a color, px value, font-family, or shadow.
- ❌ Never rename tokens during handoff.
- ❌ Never edit `.pen` files via Shell/Node (see `pencil-pen-file-editing.mdc`).
- ✅ Always emit a handoff summary listing components used, tokens referenced, and open questions.
